  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "gale-datos",
      "id": "LUG-07",
      "plano": "gale-datos",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.zSkwEUUtkNGhfXun]{Gale Sentinel Campus and Data Center}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.C7cxKf7kcAELzuJ1.JournalEntryPage.EjJ0vfVBCjTTb0QV]{A3-E02 · The Data Center}</p>\n<p><strong>Layer 3 of A3-E02: the data center.</strong> “A windowless building behind the main one. Three rooms: storage, ANOMALY training, private archive.” “A door with biometrics (fingerprint and retina) and a security mantrap. One ghoul in the control room.”</p>\n<p><strong>The infiltration strip.</strong> The service road (west) comes from the parking lot (“To the campus parking lot” region, pending: zone map) and the service yard (south) comes from the office building (region → <code>gale-sentinel</code>). The generator and chillers in the yard give cover for approaching the mantrap. Running out across the campus in front of the cameras: Thermometer +1.</p>\n<p><strong>The three security levels</strong> (the text doesn&#39;t detail them; they break down like this):</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>The mantrap.</strong> Outer door with a card reader; inner door <strong>locked</strong> with a biometric reader (Gale&#39;s or Dawson&#39;s fingerprint and retina). The two doors don&#39;t open at the same time. Forcing it: Strength + Athletics Diff. 5, and the alarm goes off. With Gale in hand (Celeste, Manipulation + Persuasion Diff. 4, or Dominate: Gale has Composure 2; Dawson, Resolve 3 and +2 dice from the Bond) the inner door opens without a roll. The ghoul in the <strong>control room</strong> watches the mantrap through the armored window.</li>\n<li><strong>The rooms</strong> (storage and testing): <strong>locked</strong> card-access doors; they open from the control room console or with the ghoul&#39;s card. From the hallway you can see inside through the glass windows: on the left, “rows of black cabinets hum under blue lights”; on the right, the wall of faces.</li>\n<li><strong>The private archive</strong>, at the end of the hallway: a <strong>locked</strong> door with its own lock, no network, isolated from everything else.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>ANOMALY cameras (at the entrances)</strong>, <code>anomaly</code> objects with no light: ① above the outer mantrap door; ② inside the mantrap; ③ in the southwest corner, covering the yard and the service road; ④ and ⑤ above the two emergency exits, outside. If the coterie didn&#39;t disable the module in layer 1, every Kindred who enters is logged (the Thermometer +1 counts only once for the whole incursion).</p>\n<p><strong>What&#39;s in each room:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Storage</strong> (west): four rows of racks. In the <strong>fireproof media safe</strong> (southwest corner), the <strong>original drive of the File, only until Night 6</strong>. On the <strong>management console</strong>, the shipping logs for the ARCHER channel with the reference <strong>SEA-0411 (P-10)</strong> and the complete <strong>DOC-07</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Testing room · ANOMALY training</strong> (east): “On one wall there&#39;s a screen with a grid of faces, hundreds of them, each with a label underneath: COLD_SUBJECT, and a number. Some of them you know from Elysium. One of them is yours.” This is the <strong>wall of faces</strong> (east wall; off on the map, two “video wall” lights turn it on). At the workstations, the <strong>cold subject database</strong> (it includes the coterie if the 3B camera recorded them in A0-E01) and <strong>DOC-11</strong>, if they don&#39;t have it. To the north, open to the room, the compute room with the GPU racks.</li>\n<li><strong>Private archive</strong> (north, at the end of the hallway): the <strong>air-gapped server</strong> with Halloway&#39;s personal archive, scanned by Pell. Copying it: Intelligence + Technology Diff. 3. The folios on “the German” (<strong>P-15</strong>): Intelligence + Investigation Diff. 4, or automatic by searching for “allemand.” This server is the one that may end up in the briefcase in A4-E03.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Alarm.</strong> If it goes off (mantrap forced, emergency exit opened), Dawson takes <strong>four minutes</strong> to arrive from the office building, and Bellevue police take <strong>twelve</strong>. The emergency exits (west and east) only open from inside and trip the alarm: they&#39;re the escape route for an assault.</p>\n<p><strong>Assault</strong> (Combat): Thermometer +2; Gale warns Halloway, who moves the original that same night if they don&#39;t take it. Dawson, alive and captured, is a witness.</p>\n<p>The hatched blocks (UPS and battery utility rooms to the southwest, cooling to the southeast) aren&#39;t played.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (4) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<div class=\"sbn-figuras\"><p><strong>Placed tokens.</strong> Hidden ones are revealed from the token layer; the ones that depend on how the night went say when.</p><ul><li>@UUID[Actor.BzNGxOAK3F6Uo56T]{Security Guard} · <em>hidden</em> (A3-E02): The control room ghoul; watches the mantrap through the window.</li></ul></div>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> To the campus parking lot (service road).</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
